WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.780
Hey, welcome to Tesla's short time, Episode 549 for July 22nd, 2026.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.600
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.420
There's a lot to cover in Tesla Land today.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.020
NHTSA's engineering analysis of FSD on 3.2 million vehicles

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.800
puts Tesla's camera-only system under final scrutiny

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.620
before any recall decision.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.380
US safety regulators escalated their investigation

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.880
into Tesla's FSD to an engineering analysis.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.020
The final phase before a potential recall.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.440
The probe covers 3.2 million vehicles

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.620
after nine low visibility crashes in fog, dust, and glare

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.200
that caused one fatality and one injury.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.920
Regulators set an August 12th deadline for Tesla

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.280
to provide the internal document radar saves us.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.840
Related emails and raw test data on the OEDR system

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:02.220
with daily fines up to $27,874 possible for non-compliance.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.140
Tesla can resolve the matter via OTA update

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.900
if it proves the software detects blinded cameras

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.660
and alerts drivers or disengages safely.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.940
Investigators are also reviewing 15 promotional claims

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:20.460
and a 2024 change that weaken the FSD degraded alert

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.800
from red to yellow with the chime muted.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.480
This development continues the tracked FSD

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.420
unsupervised program arc last reviewed on July 21,

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.120
where regulatory approval remains the key open question.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.800
Camera-only autonomy places the entire burden

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.640
of hazard detection on software

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.680
that must interpret photon counts

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.880
under every lighting and weather condition.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.460
When regulators demand proof that the system recognizes

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.120
its own blindness, the question shifts

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.060
from sensor count to algorithmic self-awareness.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.060
Tesla's approach bets that neural networks

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.700
trained on fleet data can outperform fixed hardware rules.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.740
Yet the August 12th filing will test whether

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.340
that bet has produced measurable safeguards.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.700
The internal document titled radar saves us

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.840
now sits at the center of the inquiry

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.160
because it may reveal whether engineers

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.680
once quantified the exact failure modes

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.440
that later appeared in the nine reported crashes.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.720
If the code can flag degraded visibility

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.300
and either alert the driver or disengage within milliseconds,

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.820
an over-the-air fix remains possible.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.820
Should the data fall short,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.780
the company faces a choice between

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.180
reintroducing radar or accepting limits

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.160
on where FSD can operate.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.480
That outcome carries direct cost implications.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.600
A software resolution preserves the capital

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.500
already spent on vision training

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.960
and avoids retrofitting millions of vehicles.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.520
A hardware reversal would reset

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.460
part of the 2021 decision and add expense

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.360
at a moment when cash flow is already under watch

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.280
from investors.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.940
While regulators scrutinize vision only autonomy,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.540
Tesla is quietly expanding data collection

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.800
for its other major hardware program.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.900
Tesla app code shows consent screens

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.700
for collecting video, 3D spatial data,

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.380
and tactile feedback from optimist units

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.100
operating in customer homes.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.440
The setup includes a Bluetooth robot key

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.160
with device white list and dual layer alerts

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.780
that filter developer logs into simple customer notifications

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:25.860
like low battery.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.120
This approach mirrors the FSD shadow fleet strategy

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.040
to train the robot on real household variables

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.860
such as carpet friction and fragile objects

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.980
instead of relying solely on $48 per hour motion capture

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.120
trainers in labs.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.880
It advances the optimist program.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.860
Last reviewed July 21 by moving from lab training

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.720
toward early home deployments.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.760
As optimist moves toward early customer sites,

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.580
the Robotaxi program is also locking

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.980
in physical infrastructure.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.840
San Antonio's zoning commission voted eight to two

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.720
on July 21 to recommend rezoning at 245

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.460
and 257 West Josephine Street

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:12.180
for a dedicated Robotaxi depot with 56 charging stalls.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.940
The site will serve only the autonomous fleet

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.860
and not public super chargers.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.660
With service already running in Austin, Dallas, and Houston,

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.820
this prepares expansion in a neighboring market

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.280
80 miles from Austin.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.400
This fits the CyberCab Robotaxi tracked program

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.180
where production start and regulatory approval

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.740
remain open questions.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.320
While Texas zoning moves forward,

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:38.780
California regulators have already cleared

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.600
Robotaxi operations at a major airport.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.740
Tesla's Robotaxi service now includes

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.040
San Francisco International Airport.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.680
Elon Musk noted the regulatory approval process

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.780
remains challenging.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.660
This expands the operational footprint

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.640
in an autonomous friendly region.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.380
It marks incremental progress on the commercial deployment

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.460
side of the program.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.620
On the vehicle side, Tesla continues adding

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.060
smaller but visible owner conveniences.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.520
The Tesla app now supports direct selection

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.840
and application of custom vehicle wraps

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.300
without dealer visits.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.920
Owners can preview and switch designs

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.300
through the mobile interface.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.000
This feature extends the app's role

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.140
as a unified control point across Tesla hardware.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:27.320
Tesla officially added custom wrap selection

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:28.940
directly in the mobile app.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.960
Owners gain on-demand access to design options

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.620
without third-party involvement.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.080
This integrates personalization

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.680
into the core vehicle management experience.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.580
Another recent app addition focuses on everyday safety

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.220
rather than personalization.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.140
Street parking mode positions the vehicle

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:50.720
to reduce the risk of doring by cyclists and other traffic.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:54.880
The system uses sensors to guide alignment along the curb.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.200
It adds a practical safety layer to daily driving

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.220
in urban areas.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.220
Early user posts highlight its usefulness

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.080
in real world parking scenarios.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.760
Software updates are also bringing visual polish

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.380
to current vehicle interfaces.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.660
The 2026 summer update introduces new animations

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.440
for Model 3 and Model Y interfaces.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.780
These visual changes improve driver feedback

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.360
during vehicle interactions.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.360
The update continues the pattern of software refinements

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.920
to existing vehicle lines.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.380
Owners can expect smoother on-screen responses

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:31.580
after installation.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.380
Tesla is also constructing a facility

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.820
in a small hill country town according to local filings.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.700
The project adds to the company's expanding

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.120
Texas footprint beyond Giga, Texas.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.700
Details are emerging from zoning

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.580
and permitting records in the area.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.220
Observers are tracking how it fits

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.200
into broader manufacturing or fleet support plans.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.580
The construction continues the pattern

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:58.100
of incremental site development in the state.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:01.200
Local records show activity at the location

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.680
without further public specification on exact use.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.360
This development sits alongside other Texas projects

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.660
already in operation.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.360
Beyond the US market, new competitive pressure

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:15.760
is appearing in right-hand drive regions.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.900
Expaying is evaluating the P7 for the Australian market

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:22.740
as a direct competitor to the Tesla Model 3.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.700
The move signals intensifying rivalry

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.600
in right-hand drive regions.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.120
Tesla's position in that segment

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.420
faces new pressure from Chinese entrance.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.080
The P7 is under consideration specifically

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.480
to take on the Model 3 in Australia.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.400
This evaluation comes as multiple Chinese manufacturers

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.300
explore similar market entries.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.500
Right-hand drive certification and local regulatory steps

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:49.920
remain part of the process.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.100
The development adds one more data point

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.780
to global model competition.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.020
Battery performance over time is another area

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.300
drawing attention for long-term owners.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.580
Data ranks the 2027 Model Y among vehicles

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.160
with the lowest battery degradation over time.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.920
Comparisons include the Kia Neuro and other models

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.860
showing strong capacity retention.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.240
This metric influences long-term ownership costs

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:17.620
and resale values.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.720
The ranking places the upcoming Model Y

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.720
alongside established low-degradation performers.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.560
Multiple electric vehicles were assessed

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.400
for capacity retention across years of use.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.620
The results highlight differences

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.860
in how various battery packs age

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.580
under real-world conditions.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.500
Beyond vehicles, Tesla's energy storage business

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.540
faces its own competitive pressures.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.200
Cinevoltaic's analysis shows increasing divergence

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.440
in financial strength across energy storage companies.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.500
Tesla's Megapack and Powerwall lines operate within

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.880
this competitive landscape.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.360
The gap highlights margin pressures

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.680
and consolidation risks in the sector.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.400
Investors are also watching Tesla's

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.760
near-term financial picture ahead of earnings.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:07.920
Short interest in Tesla has risen ahead of the Q2 report

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.460
as investors focus on margin trends and delivery numbers.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:15.640
The increase reflects caution around near-term profitability

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:19.500
even as longer-term autonomy and robotaxi plans

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:20.220
draw attention.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.940
Tesla will need to demonstrate concrete progress

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:26.940
on cost controls and revenue diversification

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.120
to ease that pressure.

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:31.960
Before we go, keep an eye on whether the August 12th

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.420
filing produces an OTA resolution

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.960
or extends the NHTSA review into fall.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.260
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

